{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>They did according to the word of Moses.</b> That is, not for the benefit of money but for the command of a prophet. It further intends, based on what Rambam brought in chapter 9 of Hilkhot Yesodei HaTorah, that if a prophet comes and says to Israel by the word of HaShem to transgress a single commandment as a temporary ruling, like Elijah on Mount Carmel and similar cases — one is obligated to listen to him, except for idolatry. And this is what the verse says: <b>And the children of Israel did.</b> Now since this act is an improper act — to deceive a gentile's mind, and also to rob his property — how could Israel justify doing a transgression? Therefore it says \"according to the word of Moses,\" meaning, that he was tested as a prophet, and in particular in this matter his words would be trusted as mentioned."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:27:15.662578740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}